289
00:14:05,357 --> 00:14:08,730
But let's remember, we've been here before.

290
00:14:08,730 --> 00:14:11,460
When Gutenberg introduced the printing press

291
00:14:11,460 --> 00:14:12,807
in the 15th century,

292
00:14:12,807 --> 00:14:14,430
it didn't just change

293
00:14:14,430 --> 00:14:15,960
how books were made,

294
00:14:15,960 --> 00:14:18,981
it democratized knowledge.

295
00:14:18,981 --> 00:14:21,030
For the first time,

296
00:14:21,030 --> 00:14:25,110
learning could spread beyond monasteries and the elites

297
00:14:25,110 --> 00:14:27,523
into the hands of everyday people.

298
00:14:27,523 --> 00:14:30,905
In the same way, AI has the potential

299
00:14:30,905 --> 00:14:35,635
to democratize education for our time, expanding access,

300
00:14:35,635 --> 00:14:39,963
personalized learning and accelerating discovery.

301
00:14:40,800 --> 00:14:42,540
But just like the printing press,

302
00:14:42,540 --> 00:14:46,176
its true power won't come from the technology alone.

303
00:14:46,176 --> 00:14:50,451
It will come from how we choose to use it with equity,

304
00:14:50,451 --> 00:14:54,780
ethics, and human purpose at the center.

305
00:14:54,780 --> 00:14:56,515
And that brings us

306
00:14:56,515 --> 00:15:00,273
to why we're here at the 2025 Future Summit.

307
00:15:01,290 --> 00:15:02,460
So not long ago

308
00:15:02,460 --> 00:15:04,080
after a workforce event,

309
00:15:04,080 --> 00:15:06,180
a group of students came up to me

310
00:15:06,180 --> 00:15:08,681
with a simple but profound question,

311
00:15:08,681 --> 00:15:11,624
will my education be relevant?

312
00:15:11,624 --> 00:15:15,287
That question cuts to the heart of why we're here

313
00:15:15,287 --> 00:15:18,330
'cause the answer can't just be yes.

314
00:15:18,330 --> 00:15:21,930
The answer must be your education will not only be relevant,

315
00:15:21,930 --> 00:15:26,073
it'll be life-changing, future-shaping, and world-defining.

316
00:15:26,940 --> 00:15:30,780
But here's the truth, that won't happen on its own.

317
00:15:30,780 --> 00:15:33,783
AI doesn't matter without the people

318
00:15:33,783 --> 00:15:36,960
and the infrastructure to support it.

319
00:15:36,960 --> 00:15:40,773
Cars needed roads, electricity needed power grids,

320
00:15:40,773 --> 00:15:45,143
and today, AI needs both human wisdom

321
00:15:45,143 --> 00:15:47,731
and institutional courage.

322
00:15:47,731 --> 00:15:51,810
We are the ones who will build those roads beneath the cars.

323
00:15:51,810 --> 00:15:53,280
We are the ones who will ensure

324
00:15:53,280 --> 00:15:55,890
that technology serves humanity,

325
00:15:55,890 --> 00:15:57,780
not the other way around.

326
00:15:57,780 --> 00:16:00,087
Think about what that means.

327
00:16:00,087 --> 00:16:05,087
Over 2 million students across 116 colleges

328
00:16:05,161 --> 00:16:09,270
turning to us not just for skills,

329
00:16:09,270 --> 00:16:10,863
but for hope.

330
00:16:11,940 --> 00:16:14,280
They are the reason we exist.

331
00:16:14,280 --> 00:16:16,713
They are the reason we innovate.

332
00:16:17,970 --> 00:16:21,450
The future is not something that happens to us.

333
00:16:21,450 --> 00:16:25,974
The future is something we build deliberately together

334
00:16:25,974 --> 00:16:28,020
and with purpose.

335
00:16:28,020 --> 00:16:30,090
That's what this summit is about.

336
00:16:30,090 --> 00:16:34,320
It's not just anticipating what's next but designing it.

337
00:16:34,320 --> 00:16:36,240
Not just watching change unfold,

338
00:16:36,240 --> 00:16:37,920
but leading it with courage,

339
00:16:37,920 --> 00:16:40,713
with imagination, and with heart.

340
00:16:41,610 --> 00:16:44,583
So let's not only look to the future, let's create it.

341
00:16:45,450 --> 00:16:46,768
Let's build it.

342
00:16:46,768 --> 00:16:48,720
Let's make sure that decades from now,

343
