01:49:24,000 --> 01:49:25,950
to work with a hundred institutions

2412
01:49:25,950 --> 01:49:27,090
across the United States.

2413
01:49:27,090 --> 01:49:29,970
And we're hoping a number of you here in California

2414
01:49:29,970 --> 01:49:32,190
to build out solutions that have an impact

2415
01:49:32,190 --> 01:49:34,470
on your communities.

2416
01:49:34,470 --> 01:49:36,450
Now what does that mean?

2417
01:49:36,450 --> 01:49:39,620
So when data kind worked with a mid-size MSI

2418
01:49:39,620 --> 01:49:40,650
in an urban setting,

2419
01:49:40,650 --> 01:49:41,970
a couple of years ago

2420
01:49:41,970 --> 01:49:44,970
on their challenges around graduation,

2421
01:49:44,970 --> 01:49:49,200
we helped them increase their graduation rate by 32%.

2422
01:49:49,200 --> 01:49:51,630
Now that wasn't magic,

2423
01:49:51,630 --> 01:49:55,620
that was identifying the specific problem they had

2424
01:49:55,620 --> 01:50:00,110
and not providing a generalized one model fits all solution.

2425
01:50:00,110 --> 01:50:02,130
In their case, they started to realize

2426
01:50:02,130 --> 01:50:04,770
that students who were seniors

2427
01:50:04,770 --> 01:50:06,570
were exiting without a degree,

2428
01:50:06,570 --> 01:50:09,150
but all of their student support mechanisms

2429
01:50:09,150 --> 01:50:11,040
were for undergraduates.

2430
01:50:11,040 --> 01:50:12,900
So we helped them build a model

2431
01:50:12,900 --> 01:50:14,730
that would identify those students

2432
01:50:14,730 --> 01:50:17,160
who were at risk of not graduating

2433
01:50:17,160 --> 01:50:19,950
and identify what was causing that risk.

2434
01:50:19,950 --> 01:50:23,130
What was the reason they were at risk of not graduating

2435
01:50:23,130 --> 01:50:26,070
and surface that information to their advising team.

2436
01:50:26,070 --> 01:50:27,960
So rather than their advisors looking through

2437
01:50:27,960 --> 01:50:29,370
sort of a needle in a haystack

2438
01:50:29,370 --> 01:50:31,230
to figure out which student they should support

2439
01:50:31,230 --> 01:50:32,390
at what time they,

2440
01:50:32,390 --> 01:50:34,500
we were able to use that information

2441
01:50:34,500 --> 01:50:35,880
and make direct connections

2442
01:50:35,880 --> 01:50:37,590
in a timely way with students

2443
01:50:37,590 --> 01:50:39,990
to get them the support they needed then.

2444
01:50:39,990 --> 01:50:44,220
Now that type of approach relies on transparency.

2445
01:50:44,220 --> 01:50:46,260
It relies on this co-created approach

2446
01:50:46,260 --> 01:50:48,720
of understanding what does an institution

2447
01:50:48,720 --> 01:50:51,240
need at this particular time?

2448
01:50:51,240 --> 01:50:52,950
What insights do they need

2449
01:50:52,950 --> 01:50:56,190
in order to build trust in that AI solution?

2450
01:50:56,190 --> 01:50:57,630
And how will they implement it?

2451
01:50:57,630 --> 01:51:00,960
How can this solution exist long-term

2452
01:51:00,960 --> 01:51:04,470
and be sustainable and part of their existing workflows?

2453
01:51:04,470 --> 01:51:07,170
And with DataKind, we do this,

2454
01:51:07,170 --> 01:51:09,150
we partner with institutions

2455
01:51:09,150 --> 01:51:12,090
for years at a time to build out these solutions

2456
01:51:12,090 --> 01:51:14,133
in a way that makes sense for you.

2457
01:51:14,970 --> 01:51:17,820
